  "claim_short": "2107.00492 Juha Kinnunen Kim Myyrylainen Dyadic John-Nirenberg space Coifman Rochberg type characterization. Full quantitative answer: for every finite cube Q0 and 1<p<infinity, JN_p^d(Q0) equals (JN_p^d intersect dyadic A_1) minus itself. The normalized Banach norm combines the JN seminorm with the mean. Weak-Lp embedding and the source maximal theorem make M^d bounded for this norm; Rubio de Francia iteration...",
